OL,3,GNEWSAClean-up begins as oil spill shuts
OL,4,A18 Kent beaches
OL,5,
OL,6,FEighteen beaches in Kent have been
OL,7,Fclosed due to an oil spill which the
OL,8,Flocal council said will take "many
OL,9,Fdays" to clean-up.
OL,11,F"Significant deposits of oil" were
OL,12,Ffound at beaches across the Isle of
OL,13,FThanet, including Ramsgate and the
OL,14,Fpopular tourist beaches of Margate and
OL,15,FBroadstairs.
OL,17,FThanet District Council (TDC) reported
OL,18,Fthe incident on Wednesday evening and
OL,19,Fthe Environmental Agency (EA) is
OL,20,Finvestigating. The source of the oil
OL,21,Fhas not been identified.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,322,320,200,140,0,100
